            "time": "2021-01-27T05:47:58Z",
            "id": 97022,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": {},
            "text": "For example, to allow the usage:\n\n    keys <- c(\"A\", \"B\")\n    vals <- c(\"1\", \"2\")\n    names(vals) <- keys\n    Sys.setenv(vals)\n\nThis would make Sys.setenv() a bit easier to use when the environment variable names are determined programmatically. The alternative is to use:\n\n    do.call(Sys.setenv, as.list(vals))\n\nwhich is IMHO more verbose.",
